---
title: "How the scope-based assignments claim survives Keycloak — proposed. Keycloak's token no longer carries the custom 'assignments' claim; only Academic Structure needs it, resolved via a Redis cache invalidated at the write side. PermissionResolver/CurrentAssignments/AssignmentClaim/RoleCatalog are unchanged."
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Admin
    participant UI as Roles and Permissions screen
    participant IAM as Identity and Access
    participant REDIS as Redis
    participant ACAD as Academic Structure Service
    participant PR as PermissionResolver (inside ACAD, unchanged)

    Admin->>UI: grant or override a department-scoped permission
    UI->>IAM: PATCH assignment (AssignmentService.setOverride / create / revoke)
    IAM->>IAM: write role_scope_assignments /<br/>assignment_permission_overrides (ucms.identity_access)
    IAM->>REDIS: DEL ucms:assignments:{userId}

    Note over ACAD: Later, that same user makes a request through the Gateway

    ACAD->>ACAD: UcmsJwtAuthenticationConverter extracts userId from the token's sub
    ACAD->>REDIS: GET ucms:assignments:{userId}
    alt cache hit
        REDIS-->>ACAD: cached AssignmentClaim[]
    else cache miss (just invalidated, or first request)
        ACAD->>IAM: GET /internal/assignments/{userId}<br/>Authorization: Bearer (svc-academic-structure's own client_credentials token)
        IAM-->>ACAD: current AssignmentClaim[]
        ACAD->>REDIS: SET ucms:assignments:{userId} (TTL = Keycloak access-token lifespan)
    end
    ACAD->>PR: CurrentAssignments populated — same shape as the JWT claim gave it before
    PR->>PR: canOnDepartment / isDepartmentScoped / isGlobal — identical logic to today

    Note over PR: PermissionResolver, CurrentAssignments, AssignmentClaim, RoleCatalog —<br/>none of this changes. Only where the claim comes from changes.
